hose who have believed God may be careful to maintain good works. These things are good and profitable to men;"},{"verse":9,"text":"but shun foolish questionings, genealogies, strife, and disputes about the law; for they are unprofitable and vain."},{"verse":10,"text":"Avoid a factious man after a first and second warning,"},{"verse":11,"text":"knowing that such a one is perverted and sinful, being self-condemned."},{"verse":12,"text":"When I send Artemas to you, or Tychicus, be diligent to come to me to Nicopolis, for I have determined to winter there."},{"verse":13,"text":"Send Zenas the lawyer and Apollos on their journey speedily, that nothing may be lacking for them."},{"verse":14,"text":"Let our people also learn to maintain good works to meet necessary needs, that they may not be unfruitful."},{"verse":15,"text":"All who are with me greet you. Greet those who love us in faith. Grace be with you all. Amen."}],"hasArtwork":true,"artworkUrl":"/data/images/books/titus.svg","availableLangs":["en","zh-CN"]}]